        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Function notation, evaluating and composing functions, and reading the vertex of a parabola.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Functions",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "\\( f(a) \\) substitutes \\( a \\) for \\( x \\); a composite \\( f(g(x)) \\) works inside-out. In vertex form \\( y=a(x-h)^{2}+k \\), the vertex is \\( (h,k) \\) and the axis is \\( x=h \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "figure",
        "figure": {
          "type": "fn",
          "title": "Rational Function with Asymptotes: f(x) = 1/(x - 2) + 1",
          "xrange": [-3, 7],
          "yrange": [-3, 5],
          "fns": [
            { "fn": "1/(x - 2) + 1", "color": "var(--fig-indigo-2)", "label": "f(x) = 1/(x-2) + 1" }
          ],
          "vlines": [
            { "x": 2, "color": "var(--fig-amber)", "dash": "4,3", "label": "V.A. x = 2" }
          ],
          "hlines": [
            { "y": 1, "color": "var(--fig-rose)", "dash": "4,3", "label": "H.A. y = 1" }
          ],
          "points": [
            { "x": 3, "y": 2, "label": "(3, 2)" },
            { "x": 1, "y": 0, "label": "(1, 0)" }
          ]
        },
        "caption": {
          "en": "Graph of rational function $f(x) = \\frac{1}{x - 2} + 1$. The vertical asymptote occurs where the denominator equals zero ($x = 2$, restricted from the domain). The horizontal asymptote $y = 1$ is the value approached as $x \\to \\pm\\infty$.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Slide the vertex \\( (h,k) \\) of \\( y=(x-h)^{2}+k \\). The amber dot is the vertex; the dashed line is the axis of symmetry.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
